.TH SLEEP 1
.SH NAME
sleep \- wait
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sleep
.I seconds
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sleep
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It waits at least
.I seconds
seconds, which may have decimals
.RB ( "sleep 0.25" ).
Ctrl-C ends it early.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 130 if Ctrl-C ended it; 1 without a number.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_sleep (2),
.BR sh (1)
